+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use an LRU (Least Recently Used) eviction policy combined with a 300-second TTL: cache entries are evicted based on recency of access, and any entry is additionally expired after 300 seconds regardless of access pattern, giving both memory efficiency and freshness guarantees.
